	abstract = {Websites and blogs are being captured as tools of collecting real time information nowadays. Conversely, the high growth of blogs on cloud servers has created huge volume of information, which contains thoughts, opinions, and assessments. Accordingly, methods of extracting practical knowledge based on huge volumes of information, categorizing it, and predicting the behavior of end-users or their feelings are urgently required. In the modern world, people sharing their ideas on social media platforms happen instantly. This data can hardly be analyzed and conclusions can be made. Automated machine learning techniques still do not make it easy to extract meaningful concepts out of data. In this paper, we propose a new model to embed information between two adjacent words by combining word embedding with BERT. We have used BERT-CNN model in searching offensive language identification and attempted to increase the accuracy, our model employs rectified linear units, normalizing and dropout technologies. Collected Offensive data will be evaluated into different 3 - stages (A, B, C), at C stage result is 81% perfect with no error. © 2025 IEEE.},
