	affiliations = {Karunya Institute of Technology and Sciences, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Coimbatore, TN, India},
	abstract = {Hatred speech detection in social network is now a critical issue with the increased prevalence of harmful online content. In this work, a study among three models - Bidirectional Encoders Representations from Transformers (BERT), Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP), and Support Vector Machine (SVM), in contextual hatred speech detection, has been presented. A labeled Kaggle hate speech input is employed to fine-tune and test the models. Evaluation measures such as precision, recall, f1-score, accuracy and confusion matrix are used to evaluate the model. The output shows that BERT is superior to MLP and SVM in detecting context-dependent hatred speech, owing to the former's ability to learn subtle language patterns. This work highlights the importance of circumstantial awareness in hatred speech detection. © 2025 IEEE.},
