	abstract = {The exponential expansion of social media networking platforms has magnified the dissemination of hate speech, thereby requiring strong recognition systems to minimize its influence. The present work offers a comparative examination of many prediction models for the recognition of hate speech using social media data, employing Artificial Intelligence (AI) methodologies. The paper intends to assess the efficiency of several Machine Learning (ML) and Deep Learning (DL) algorithms for accurately detecting hate speech. The various strategies are evaluated using known datasets and measures including accuracy, recall, precision, and Fl-score. In addition, useful insights on the most effective methods for identifying hate speech are presented. The findings suggest that deep learning approaches are exceptionally effective at catching the contextual nuances of hate speech. Al-based hate speech detection apps improve accuracy and efficiency. Such systems are critical for creating a safer and more inclusive online. © 2025 IEEE.},
