	affiliations = {Neil Gogte Institute of Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Hyderabad, TS, India; The Islamic University, Najaf, Department of Computers Techniques Engineering, Najaf, Najaf, Iraq; Nitte Meenakshi Institute of Technology, Department of Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, Bengaluru, KA, India; Dhanalakshmi Srinivasan College of Engineering and Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Chennai, TN, India; New Prince Shri Bhavani College of Engineering and Technology, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Chennai, TN, India},
	abstract = {In recent years, toxic comment detection evolved as important in detecting hatred and harmful content present in user-generated content. However, a few challenges are raised in detecting toxic comments like context sensitivity and missing toxic content. To overcome these issues, improved Bi-directional Long Short-Term Memory (Bi-LSTM) is proposed for toxic comment detection. Initially, data is preprocessed with lemmatization and stop words removal methods for converting the texts to its base form and eliminates the common words respectively. Then, the Word to Vector (Word2Vec) technique converts the words into a dense vector representation by capturing semantic relationships and contextual meanings. Finally, improved Bi-LSTM is employed for detecting the toxic comments by capturing both past as well as future context with its bidirectional architecture and focuses on important words within the context dynamically. From the results, proposed Improved Bi-LSTM model attained better outcomes in terms of accuracy (acc) of 94.32%, precision (pr) of 98.07%, and recall of 95.98% compared to existing Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN)-BiLSTMs. © 2025 IEEE.},
